{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513645-v20-help-character-concept-idea-to-flesh-out","id":1513645,"title":"V20 help character concept idea to flesh out","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-02T07:31:58-07:00","id":1513645,"title":"V20 help character concept idea to flesh out","content":"So, first, i am looking to optimise the theme of the character, it doesnt have to be effective just comply with the rules of v20 (dark ages and modern as source are fine) though i would appreciate tipps on what would be a really bad idea for playability so that it isnt completly broken or useless.<br /> <br /> second, i know it will sound very special snowflaky but i can just stress out that i find the concept intruiging and hope to sell it to STs even though its a bit out there.<br /> <br /> A while ago i made a homebrew ice based discipline as we dont have anything like that in the offical games and many great people here helped me to grind it into something actually fun and usable but it is homebrew and when i am trying to play instead of using it for NPCs as ST obviously no one allows it in.<br /> <br /> So the idea is to create an ice - cold - themed vampire according to the rules. The short backstory idea was that the character is embraced just before freezing to death to save him to explain the theme.<br /> An option is a scientist in the arctic circle, or a survival enthusiast in canada, a victim of the mafia locked into a freezer, someone who went overboard in the winter and was in icy waters for many hours or a mountain climber surprised by a strom....many options for potential sire backgrounds. Could even come from pretty much anywhere as long as the region becomes sufficiently cold during winter and for metaphysical reasons i like the idea of embrace happening on the 21st to solstice.<br /> Who knows maybe there was something supernatural going on like a Kolduns way of wind sorcery, or a true mage playing around with weather magick, or some fae playing a nasty trick...something to explain the theme, the character might not even be aware of. Heck it could be a technocrat that thought creating Meis freeze gun from overwatch is a fun idea and he was the first one shot with it.<br /> <br /> So obviously skills and attributes would vastly depend on the background but i guess withstanding cold for long should require 3 dots in stamina or even 4 just because he needs to really be submerged in the cold for long to explain the effects better, and while he would have died without the embrace, he shouldnt just die from a breeze, similarily survival might be a skill to put some dots into, to represent knowledge how to survive the cold.<br /> <br /> Discipline wise i cant really figure out much. I mean yeah Kolduns do have way of wind, which has at least 2 ice themed and cold sorceries but Kolduns are also very rare and not many groups accept them for PCs. Similiarily i thought the true Brujah discipline of Temporis is a great fit with the whole stasis and &quot;freezing time&quot; aspect as ultimately, cold is a lack of movement on the atomic level and absolute cold means absolute stand still, you can literally freeze time, in theory. But Temporis is only for true Brujah as far as i understand it and no chance to aquire it as another clan, maybe caitiff?<br /> i also thought obtenebration could be kinda thematic as in world of darkness the abyss is described as very cold and dark place, and fortitude could represent some kind of hardened body due to the ice (as cold usually increases the hardness of any material) celerity would work if it would be more of a &quot;everyone else moves slower not you faster&quot; thing but that is exactly what temporis does.<br /> <br /> Havent found anything in necromancy or thaumaturgy though. Potence is a stretch as well but frozen things hit harder...because they literally are harder so...well...kinda...somewhatish.In mean doesnt need to hit with more force but harder objects transfer more kinetic energy.<br /> <br /> Merits is tough cause i have not found a single merit that goes in that direction. Flaws however i have found:<br /> <br /> - Cold breeze and Touch of frost (1 point each) that even make sense in combination and thematicly, however they make it very hard to hide ones true nature, in special when hunters are about.<br /> - Curse in special the arcane curse from the Tremere gives options too, i am thinking of something like a capadocian like curse that you look like a frozen corpse, maybe with actual ice forming in the hair, or frost on the skin, or unusual icy eye color, or a permament sound of moving glaciers when the character moves all of which add to the dead giveaway thing.<br /> - Grip of the damned could be represented as 4 point flaw of a cold kiss, that lacks all the warmth and passion when vampires are usually feeding and lead to a ice cold shock like sensation for victims making the feeding into a horrible experience rather than a pleasurable one.<br /> i dont know if albinism exists as a flaw, could fit though.<br /> <br /> question is how likely it would be to get these approved as many of those flaws basicly just do the same thing, being a dead giveaway that you are not human.<br /> <br /> Which brings me to clans. I think someone so obviously a vampire can not be in the camarilla, it would have to be a sabbath. There is no clan that has such a theme, but Gangrel sounds like it could happen and the flaw could manifest in white fur and polar bear or arctic wolf features.<br /> <br /> Similiar Tzimisce sounds at least cold hearted, somewhat, true Brujah do have stasis powers, Lasombra have the darkness...it could be a weird caitiff/pander type as well though again cherry picking disciplines is also usually not received well.<br /> <br /> For paths of enlightenment that could fit i have NO clue. Just that humanity is kinda not working<br /> <br /> So i know this is a weird request but id really appreciate some help XD Thank you in advance. And if you want to tell me that my idea is totally stupid, thats fine too, just give some reasons beyond &quot;cause its stupid&quot; =)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4364,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","user":"Orkar","date":". 06-02-2023, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T08:42:05-07:00","id":1513652,"title":"","content":"You could be a <b>Maeghar</b><br /> All Maeghar have some physical feature indicating their fae nature, which can range from the subtle (snow white skin and ebony hair) to the blatant (six arms).<br /> You can pass your discipline and/or featrues as the Mytherceria version and fae heritage<br /> Recognizing the need for some form of support in a dark and dangerous world, many Maeghar have fallen in with the Tal'Mahe'Ra. but you could be in any sect, or just be independent<br /> OR be a member of a Drowned Legacy; those half-cryptid vampires have strange powers to begin with, The Karai Pyrahe are native from Peru to Argentina with the powers to imitate the sounds of any creature, walk without making a sound or leaving a trace, and contort their way through impossibly small spaces. The Kalku are native to Argentina and Chile. They are rumored to possess a Discipline that allows them physical control over the blood in their victims, puppeteering them according to their will. The Lostundo can take on the traits and appearance of those they feed from, using this ability to lure their prey outside of the safety of their homes. The Titlacauan are a Legacy without a clear point of origin, being generally active in high society. Their unique gift gives them power over reflective surfaces, allowing them to peer through reflections, and ultimately pass between them. Unhudo resemble corpses mummified by intense heat and they use their appearance while lying completely still to attract inquisitive mortals that want to investigate them. In the modern age, their ability to climb up walls like a spider makes them effective predators in the city.<br /> Your discipline and/or looks wouldn't be in the top three strange Drwoned Legacy powers and they are totally undocumented, so could be anything\u200b<br /> As for the path?<br /> Path of Rathmonicus / Path of the Scorched Heart maybe?<br /> Many True Brujah search for a state they call\u201cPerfection.\u201d Just what this state of being really is, no one can answer completely. It is commonly held that it is the perfect union of mind and body and a state of pure logical reasoning and pragmatic rationality. Some True Brujah (such as Rathmonicus and his followers) espouse the purging of emotions as a key to Perfection, while other hold that while strong emotions might be a hindrance, one cannot be perfect if one is devoid of emotions.\u200b<br /> Or Via Venator Umbra, more commonly known as the Path of the Grey Hunter (from Road of the Beast)<br /> <br /> For a more... .esoteric aproach?<br /> The Path of Making from Vampire Twentieth Anniversary Edition: The Dark Ages could also work maybe? - For those on the Path of Making, Lilith is the mother of monsters, and they strive to emulate her by example. The divine (or infernal) children of Lilith, the incubi and succubi, interbred with mortals, and followers of this Path seek out mortals with such divine bloodlines for study. They also do their best to create their own monsters, though the exact nature of such creation is highly personal and varied, and may involve magic, infernalism, or simply careful breeding.<br /> Or Path of Veils from the same book - Those who follow the Path of Veils revere Lilith as the rebellious mother of monsters, who claimed to be God's equal and who was betrayed by Caine. They reject both Cainite orthodoxy and the Christian principles on which it is based. To them, Lilith is a symbol of liberty, and they will be free when Cainite society is destroyed.<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T08:53:26-07:00","id":1513654,"title":"","content":"Lots of ideas indeed thanks =) the kyasid actually reminds me of another flaw to take - blood has to be cooled before drinking, as in poured into a container and refrigerated, may go along with the iron stomache merit to take more nourishment from blood packs and dead blood. Or since we are at it maybe he has to eat the blood in form of frozen blood, that would add more serious issues, you can argue &quot;cool&quot; blood is relative and you might carry a bloodpack with you without it getting &quot;warm&quot; but frozen? thats difficult outside of winter","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4364,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","user":"Orkar","date":". 06-02-2023, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T08:55:41-07:00","id":1513655,"title":"","content":"Simplest way to give your character ice powers is make him a thaumaturge: you were a scientist working on cryo-something before you were embraced by a Tremere interested in your intellect and your field. <b>Thaumaturgy kinda works on the principle of 'if it exists, there's magic for it'</b> so making an ice path (probably by cannibalizing specific powers from other paths and slapping on an ice theme) isn't much of a stretch if you know your ST enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T09:12:33-07:00","id":1513659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513645-v20-help-character-concept-idea-to-flesh-out?p=1513655#post1513655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simplest way to give your character ice powers is make him a thaumaturge: you were a scientist working on cryo-something before you were embraced by a Tremere interested in your intellect and your field. <b>Thaumaturgy kinda works on the principle of 'if it exists, there's magic for it'</b> so making an ice path (probably by cannibalizing specific powers from other paths and slapping on an ice theme) isn't much of a stretch if you know your ST enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>while true its not much of a stretch it sadly is one and im not sure it would fly =/ best is to stick to rules that already exist, while an ST can still say no its easier to argue if its officially possible, and better if its not too much removed from &quot;normal&quot; as in - true brujah sounds great but that is already pretty exotic","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T09:29:53-07:00","id":1513660,"title":"","content":"To be honest an Embraced Dr. Victor Fries sounds awesome and a whole Gotham by Night premise <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Back to your discipline...<br /> It is not from Vampire (or World of Darkness) per se, but <b>Cryokinesis </b>from Trinity could work for your favor - I mean it is a White Wolf setting after all<br /> <br /> \u2022 Thermal Screen - The first thing any self-respecting Legionnaire learns is how to protect himself. By drawing in ambient heat, the psion can shield himself from the worst effects of exposure, cold damage or even from cryokinetic attacks. This effect can make the psion\u2019s immediate surroundings even colder as the psychokinetic absorbs more and more heat energy.<br /> \u2022\u2022 Hypothermic Blast - Hypothermic Blast is a term used to describe the phenomenon in which a psion focuses a quick blast of supercooled air at a target. The sudden freezing effect visibly frosts the air between psion and subject, and can slow the target\u2019s metabolism or even cause frostbite.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Flash Freeze - The psion slows the motion of free liquids, freezing them to solids in the space of seconds. This effect can be used on such high temperature liquids as boiling water or molten metal, although the higher the substance\u2019s current temperature the more challenging this becomes. Flash Freeze is not effective against living beings or other complex organisms. This power may also be used for less direct effects, such as condensing and freezing surrounding water vapor (a psion could Fill his drink with ice and dehumidify the room at the same time).<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Heat Sink - Heat Sink allows a psychokinetic to extinguish open fires with a glance. He psionically halts the fire\u2019s molecular motion, cooling even a red-hot ember. A skilled psion can snuff a bonfire in an instant. Not even warm ash remains.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Cryofreeze - This effect is comparable to that of a liquid nitrogen bath. The psion can freeze flesh or blood as well as wood, plastic or metal into a brittle, supercold state. This power inflicts severe frostbite or hypothermia in seconds when used on living beings. Not even heavily bundled targets are immune - the effect simply ignores any layers of clothing and focuses on the person within.<br /> <br /> By any means Cryokinesis is not strong, but easly could be mimiced, either by Thaumaturgy as MyWifeIsScary wrote, or a specialized branch of Abyss Mysticism (calling the cold of the darkness between the stars, or the void outside reality), Necromancy (similarly, the cold of Death) or even Daimonion (level 3 Conflagration draws out the destructive essence of the Beyond - it could be destructive cold while level 6 Glimpse the Gulf Beyond: Open a rift to the Beyond - mentally and phisically destruciv distortion/tear in reality)<br /> And of course you already have your discipline worked out, just wanted to pointed ot, similar could exist and tere are similar examples to it - Wendigo Gifts are great example as their level 5 that freezes the heart. But they especially have many ice/codl realted gifts as other Fera<br /> The Koldunic Way of Wind 2nd power is Biting Gale - A koldun creates frigid winds that slow or freeze a target. Way of Sorrow's level 5 is The Starvation of Marena - A koldun can create a frosty gale that blast the victim and leaves him emaciated as if he had just survived the coldest of winters.<br /> <br /> So you are not in the realm of &quot;such power don't exist&quot; don't worry<br /> Either of those could work as a base from you can build up your own powerset <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b<br /> \u200b <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T12:38:29-07:00","id":1513684,"title":"","content":"i am mindblown right now XD i totally forgot about wendigo and wasnt even aware cryokinesis is a thing (never touched trinity cause i wasnt really aware of it)<br /> <br /> thank you for the great tips =)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}